## One capability and one candidate

Implement a general read-only relation for two finite, connected, closed, orientable, non-self-intersecting triangular shells, including nonconvex geometry and through-holes. It must answer the original assembly's solid classification and, with existing surface distance, identify all penetrating parts and the nearest separated part. Do not recognize object names, ring parameters, twelve-sided structure, special world axes or fixture answers.

Keep existing geometry_safety/solid_relation/write execution semantics intact. The old solid_relation means overlap at 1e-9 m tolerance; it must not silently become zero-tolerance topology, and pair_relation must not receive invented signed depths. Add one clearly named read-only fact, preferably closed_solid_relation, to the existing task interface with explicit zero-tolerance classification of represented closed solids: separated, touching, penetrating (positive-volume interior overlap). State the geometry scope once in normal tool/result metadata. Do not build a new service, permission tier, solver framework, global MTV, or write action. Existing normal task query remains the entry; use existing surface_proximity for separated distances and current object/cache binding.

## Algorithm direction

Reuse existing exact triangle predicates and integer frame; surface_geometry has an exact BVH that can be minimally extended to cross-surface candidate traversal. Combine boundary-intersection analysis with a bounded exact point-in-solid/containment test. A positive surface gap alone cannot reject containment; a zero gap alone cannot prove penetration; vertex-only testing misses crossing solids. Choose a deterministic degeneracy policy and return explicit unknown when it cannot establish the promised classification. Do not use unchecked floating winding thresholds or approximate Barnes-Hut values as exact answers. Treat self-intersecting/open/nonmanifold/unsupported multiple-shell inputs honestly.

Aim for a lean implementation from the first candidate: BVH pruning and early sufficient witnesses, shared preparation within a query, existing successful pair-cache reuse keyed by complete current geometry and algorithm version. Avoid repeated mesh validation when existing sound prepared data suffices. Record actual predicate/candidate work where cheaply available. Do not launch an unrelated cache/residency redesign, raise budgets to hide quadratic work, or add layers solely for this experiment.

## Acceptance

Use the unchanged original assembly and accepted Decimal80 truth. Initial and unchanged: 02 separated about .01 m, 03 penetrating, 04 separated about .04 m, nearest separated 02. Changed original four-point patch: 02/03 penetrating, 04 separated and nearest. Check precise distances with the existing nonzero error bound, not rounded example numbers. Preserve original source, rotation, all candidates and AABB-invariant edit.

Targeted analytic tests must distinguish hole containment from material containment, crossing boundaries with neither mesh's vertices inside the other, face/edge/point tangency and coincident/ambiguous boundaries, ordinary rotations/translations and swapped objects/orientation, invalid topology and numerical/work-deadline unknown. Do not write tests that merely restate implementation. Exact represented-geometry answers and source uncertainty must not be conflated. Retain relevant old convex/P1 and task-entry/cache regression checks; run the necessary checks once per meaningful change, not the full unrelated matrix repeatedly.

Freeze at most one coherent product candidate and source identity before actual QA. Reuse the existing private controlled loader/stdio harness. One private NativeSession, original deadline at most 600 seconds without renewal, at most 9 public observations and 16 total physical RPC including captures, admin readback, one original QA patch and close. No new model consumers. Use the three states with the same current candidate; each pair query may request the new relation plus needed existing distance facts. Capture/query and close all count. Prepare before opening the session; reserve cleanup. If the required facts remain unsupported, stop further repeated qualification and explain the precise remaining gap. No second candidate or new session to chase a score.

Use the matching CLOSED_SOLID_WINDOW.json and root STATE for the exclusive resource window. Full implementation budget 90 minutes from receipt; original private session still 600 seconds. Keep all failed attempts and actual unknowns. If a general solution cannot be made correct within this scope, return the incomplete candidate/precise obstacle, rather than expanding to arbitrary solids, decomposition or new write domains.

